  "item.simpleoctets.guide_book": "Simple Octets Guide",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.1.title": "Simple Octets",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.1": "Octets - half-block cubes of every wood, of every block with stairs and slabs and of the melon - cut in the Shapecutter (Simple Blocks; without it in the stonecutter), placed into the clicked corner and mixed in one cell.",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.2.title": "Octets: half-block cubes of every material",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.2": "An octet is a cube of 0.5 x 0.5 x 0.5 blocks.",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.3.title": "Octets: half-block cubes of every material",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.3": "Every wood (planks), every block with stairs and slabs and a set of building colors without stairs (terracotta, metal and mineral blocks, logs and stems, wool, concrete) has its own octet with the texture",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.4.title": "Octets: half-block cubes of every material",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.4": "of its block; up to eight octets fill one block cell.",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.5.title": "Shapecutter and back",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.5": "The Shapecutter of Simple Blocks cuts 8 octets from the full block of their material (wood octets from the planks); with Simple Blocks the Vanilla stonecutter has no octet recipes.",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.6.title": "Shapecutter and back",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.6": "Without Simple Blocks the stonecutter cuts them instead. 8 octets of one material craft back into the block (shapeless);",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.7.title": "Shapecutter and back",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.7": "the crafting recipe and the stonecutter cut unlock in the recipe book once you hold the block or the octet (the saw has no recipe book).",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.8.title": "Mixed cells",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.8": "Octets of different materials share one cell: the cell becomes the mixed octet cell, which keeps the material of each octet in its block entity, and turns back into a pure cell as soon as one material is left.",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.9.title": "Melon octets",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.9": "Sneak + right-click a block with a melon slice to place it as a melon octet (without sneaking it",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.10.title": "Melon octets",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.10": "is eaten). The cell shows rind outside and flesh on the cut faces and drops one melon slice per octet.",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.11.title": "Octets of other mods' blocks",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.11": "Octets of another mod's blocks exist only while that mod is loaded, with their recipes; without it neither the cells nor the recipes are there.",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.12.title": "Worlds from SimpleBuilding",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.12": "The octets were SimpleBuilding's before split stage 6. Placed cells, octet items, the mixed cell and its",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.13.title": "Worlds from SimpleBuilding",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.13": "block entity, the recipes in the recipe book and their unlocks keep working under the new simpleoctets: ids;",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.14.title": "Worlds from SimpleBuilding",
  "simpleoctets.guide.page.14": "the next save writes the new ids.",
  "quests.simpleoctets.start.title": "Welcome to Simple Octets",
  "quests.simpleoctets.start.subtitle": "Your free guide",
  "quests.simpleoctets.start.welcome.title": "A free guide",
  "quests.simpleoctets.start.welcome.description": "Craft or pick up a crafting table and claim the Simple Octets Guide as a reward. You can also craft it from a book and a stonecutter."
}
